ts or progressives  the if my name comes up they snap right  back to basically labeling me a right  winger that  everything is black and white your  forests are against us you're either a  left winger or right winger and they  keep throwing me to the other camp  even though socially I'm as liberal as  you could get just because I'm not in  lockstep with them they amongst  themselves they're always calling me  your right winger which is really  annoying if that that pisses me off  because it isn't true and but it's I  just got used to it I don't know what  else to say you know you used to give me  fits but I've just gotten used to that  how I wound up working for a reason I  was working for a website called suck  suck calm and then the suck went out of  business but many of their contributors  worked for recent magazine so it seemed  like it was a natural thing for me to do  something similar for a recent magazine  that I was doing for suck which mainly  was covering an event doing my own comic  book style reporting on the little  things like cartoon journalism the most  recent piece I did for a reason it was  about minimum-security women's prison it  didn't change my feelings about the drug  war personally I feel like all drugs  should be decriminalized because every  single woman I talked to there where it  was in prison at least partly for drugs  either they were caught holding or  selling it or else they were stealing  our prostituting themselves to pay for  drugs but still what made the  situation's so complicated is that a lot  of those women felt like the jail was  the best thing that could have happened  to them they couldn't imagine kicking  drugs besides going to prison  of course nine times out of ten they  could go back on drugs once they get out  most of them I can't give you a  percentage but let's say ninety percent  come from a world where going in and out  of prison being on welfare just being  Ward's of the state to some degree is  the norm not just for themselves and not  just for their families but these entire  communities they live in it's this other  part of America that thankfully I'm not  a part of but it's almost all these  women are right now I have to say it  doesn't seem to be a scary time  politically with the state of the  economy and and the government being  bankrupt I can't help but feel  pessimistic about what's going to happen  next especially since the last ten years  of  bad thing that happened I pretty much  predicted but then I have to say there  have been times in the past where also  where I was even more convinced that  things were going to get worse I can't  everyone the 90 started for some reason  I was convinced the 90s were going to be  worse than the 80s but they were better  which surprised me they were better in  almost every way at least in my opinion  you know so then I just got lazy and  naturally assumed that the the arts  would be better than the nineties and  they weren't they were worse
 

